# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  .env.example — copy this to .env and fill in your own values.
#
#    cp .env.example .env      (or:  copy /Y .env.example .env)
#
#  .env is gitignored and is where REAL credentials belong.
#  settings.js (committed) reads these variables and falls back
#  to harmless placeholders when one is missing.
#
#  Every value below is optional — the bot starts without them,
#  but the related commands will not work until they are set.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── AI providers ─────────────────────────────────────────────
GROQ_API_KEY=            # .ai / whisper transcription — console.groq.com
GEMINI_API_KEY=          # .ai image generation — aistudio.google.com

# ── Cloudflare Workers AI (image fallback #1) ────────────────
# dash.cloudflare.com → Workers AI → Use REST API
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# ── Command-specific keys ────────────────────────────────────
GIPHY_API_KEY=           # .gif — developers.giphy.com
OMDB_API_KEY=            # .imdb — omdbapi.com/apikey.aspx
TENOR_API_KEY=           # .emojimix — console.cloud.google.com (Tenor API)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=      # .stickertelegram — create your own with @BotFather

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=        # any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1
# TMDB_API_KEY=          # .tmdb — themoviedb.org/settings/api

# ── Outbound proxy pool (media downloads) ────────────────────
# WHY YOU MIGHT NEED THIS: YouTube blocks by IP. A datacenter host
# (a free panel, a VPS) is usually already flagged, and then EVERY
# player client fails with "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" —
# run `.ytdiag` to confirm that is what you are hitting.
#
# ⚠️  A DATACENTER PROXY WILL NOT HELP. Free and cheap proxy lists are
#     themselves datacenter IPs, already abused and already blocked.
#     What works is a residential or mobile proxy.
#
# Comma-separated. Both forms are accepted:
#   http://user:pass@host:port
#   socks5://host:port
# Leave unset for a direct connection.
# PROXIES=

# ── RapidAPI YouTube fallback (optional) ─────────────────────
# A LAST-RESORT fallback for hosts whose IP YouTube blocks. yt-dlp stays
# primary; this is only reached when yt-dlp has already failed.
#
# WHY: yt-dlp fetches from THIS host's IP. On a flagged datacenter IP every
# player client is refused ("Sign in to confirm you're not a bot") and no
# client, cookie or plugin choice fixes it — run `.ytdiag` to confirm. This
# service fetches from its own IPs, so it works where yt-dlp cannot.
#
# ⚠️  FREE TIER IS 100 REQUESTS/MONTH — roughly three a day. A safety net,
#     not a primary source. Paid plans start at $12/month.
# ⚠️  Third-party dependency: it will eventually rot (three earlier ones did).
# ⚠️  Video via this path is capped at the best MUXED mp4 (often 360p), because
#     it has no ffmpeg merge step.
# RAPIDAPI_KEY=
# RAPIDAPI_HOST=youtube-media-downloader.p.rapidapi.com

# ── Free WARP tunnel (optional, for IP-blocked hosts) ────────
# If `.ytdiag` shows YouTube blocks EVERY player client on your host's IP
# (datacenter / free panel / VPS), this gives a FREE, unlimited way around it:
# it runs Cloudflare WARP as a local SOCKS5 proxy. Cloudflare's egress IPs are
# NOT blocked by YouTube, and `usque` does it in userspace (no root needed — so
# it works inside a Pterodactyl container).
#
# What enabling it does on first start:
#   1. downloads the usque binary (checksum-verified) into .warp/
#   2. registers a free Cloudflare account (this accepts Cloudflare's Terms of
#      Service on your behalf — see lib/warpProxy.js)
#   3. starts a SOCKS5 proxy on 127.0.0.1:1080 and points the bot at it
#
# Leave this OFF unless you actually need it. It downloads a third-party binary.
# WARP=1
# WARP_PORT=1080   # only if you need a different local port
# WARP_HTTP2=1     # only if your host blocks UDP (QUIC) — forces HTTP/2 over TCP

# ── Extra yt-dlp arguments (escape hatch) ────────────────────
# Whitespace-separated, applied to EVERY yt-dlp call. Use this to apply
# a fix without waiting for a code change.
#
# The most useful case: YouTube blocks IPv4 but not IPv6 (they are
# different addresses). `.ytdiag` tests both and says if that is your
# situation — if it is, force IPv6:
# YTDLP_EXTRA_ARGS=-6

# ── Runtime tuning (optional) ────────────────────────────────
# POT_PROVIDER_DIR=~/bgutil-ytdlp-pot-provider/server
# POT_PROVIDER_PORT=4416
# DL_HEALTH_INTERVAL_MS=1200000
# YTDLP_BIN=yt-dlp
# FFMPEG_PATH=
